        "text": "Based on your resume, since your experience is mainly in the hospitality sector, the suitable opportunities in Japan may initially be in back-end hospitality roles such as housekeeping or other positions where communication with native Japanese people is comparatively limited. The final job role will also depend on the interview and the requirements of the employer.\n\nHowever, after completing one year of employment in Japan, you can choose to change your sector if you meet the requirements. For changing to a particular sector, you will generally need to pass the N3 Japanese language examination and the relevant skill test for that sector in Japan.",
